From eed686c6fa19ae505b3fb142093a3672e2978ea8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:30:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Release is a bank placeholder option, not a zero-count option

Reported from play 2026-09-21: three items in the Shantay Pass shop offered
"Release". They are its bucket, bowl and jug, all stocked at 0.

The placeholder menu tested only `iop != null && invSlotObjCount[slot] == 0`,
and a zero count is not unique to a placeholder - a shop line stocked at zero
looks exactly the same on the wire. 35 shop invs in the content carry 272 of
them between them, so this was every shop in the game and not a Shantay quirk.

It now also requires the component's first option to begin with "Withdraw".
That is the bank grid's wording, and it is a deliberate choice over a hardcoded
component id: an id in here is a number nobody editing the content would think
to look at.

THE GATE IS NOT EXACT AND THE CONTENT SIDE SAYS SO. Four components carry
Withdraw options, and the party drop chest's five are spelled identically to
the bank's, so no wording can separate them. What makes it correct is that only
the bank ever holds a zero count - placeholders are the only thing that makes
one, and shops carry Value and Buy. banktab_sim.py in the content repo checks
exactly that, and fails if a new component grows Withdraw options, because a
check in here could never go red when the content renames one.

Compiled: javac over the whole tree, 82 classes, no errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dc7giZ7Qnh4qy1CYPTDrmH
---
 src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java b/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java
index e7187eb..cb57a8e 100644
--- a/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java
+++ b/src/main/java/jagex2/client/Client.java
@@ -13881,11 +13881,25 @@ public class Client extends GameShell {
 												}
 											}
 										}
-										if (var13.iop != null && var13.invSlotObjCount[realSlot] == 0) {
+										if (var13.iop != null && var13.invSlotObjCount[realSlot] == 0
+												&& var13.iop[0] != null && var13.iop[0].startsWith("Withdraw")) {
 											// Bank placeholders: the stub is not a stack you can take any of, so the
 											// five Withdraw entries are replaced by the one thing you can do to it.
 											// It rides op 1, so [inv_button1] is where the script picks it up - and
 											// the script has to test for a placeholder BEFORE it withdraws.
+											//
+											// AND ONLY IN THE BANK. A zero count is not unique to a placeholder: a
+											// shop line stocked at 0 looks exactly the same on the wire, and 35 shop
+											// invs in the content carry 272 of them between them. Without the option
+											// test every one of those items offered "Release" - reported from play
+											// 2026-09-21 against the Shantay Pass shop, whose bucket, bowl and jug
+											// are all stocked at 0.
+											//
+											// The gate is the component's own first option rather than its id,
+											// because an id hardcoded here is a number nobody maintaining the
+											// content would ever think to look at. The contract is that the bank
+											// grid's options are the Withdraw ones, and banktab_sim.py checks that
+											// from the content side - a client-only check could never go red there.
 											this.menuOption[this.menuSize] = "Release @lre@" + var23.field811;
 											this.menuAction[this.menuSize] = 9;
 											this.menuParamA[this.menuSize] = var23.field845;
